note bottom of LD #F1F5F9
  Every generator's signature is
  <latex>f(\&\,\texttt{LanguageDef}) \rightarrow \text{artifact}</latex>.
  The seam is already clean; this FIPS adds a
  second **producer**, not a new seam. Verified
  in §I.2 against macros/src/lib.rs.
  ——
  **TWO arrows terminate here, and the diagram says so.**
  The one-decoder property is scoped to the arrow this
  FIPS adds: <latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> is the sole decoder **from a value**.
  ""language!"" still parses Rust tokens directly, because
  routing it through the value form would require every
  construct to have a v1 value spelling — and §IV.12's
  gaps G-1 … G-3 say **two** shipped languages do not:
  ""RhoCalc"" (G-1 and G-3) and ""CalcLambda"" (G-2). The
  boundary is narrower than "everything with Rust in it":
  ""Calculator"" and ""LedTest"" carry native bodies and
  would route through the value form as ""(&#34;src&#34;, &#34;Rust&#34;, …)"".
  The macro parser is therefore **frozen**, and the
  residual drift risk is bounded by §VI.3's corpus
  fingerprint test rather than declared impossible.
end note

